Cell["\<\
Animate the above plots to illustrate the diffusion of heat into a \
1-dimensional rod as a function of time.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"628343d9-6220-4def-8bf3-1a6d6c30301f"],

Cell["\<\
Observe that the above animation has the space interval  0 \[LessEqual] x \
\[LessEqual] 10 subdivided into 20 intervals (displayed as narrow vertical \
rectangular boxes).  Flux by diffusion transfers heat from a warmer \"box\" \
to an adjacent cooler \"box\".  Therefore, heat is transferred from \"box\" \
to \"box\" to \"box\" to \"box\"... etc.   The rate of heat transfer between \
two \"boxes\" (i.e. the heat flux between two adjacent \"boxes\") depends \
upon the temperature gradient (i.e. the temperature differential between \
adjacent \"boxes\").  Therefore the larger the temperature gradient between \
adjacent \"boxes\" the faster heat will flow.  Carefully observing the above \
animation indicates that for this specific problem, the temperature \
differential at the left boundary is the largest when t = 0.  For later times \
t > 0, the temperature differential between adjacent \"boxes\" becomes less \
and therefore the rate of heat transfer becomes less as well.  It should be \
clear for this specific problem, that as the temperature becomes more uniform \
across the length of the rod (i.e. the temperature gradient approaches 0) \
then the rate of heat flux also slows to 0.  Therefore, it would take an \
infinite amount of time for the temperature profile to reach equilibrium \
conditions.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39846031921*^9, 3.398460320408*^9}, {3.398460634066*^9, 
  3.398460634234*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e528dd86-f540-4f3a-92c7-044f7e5993b7"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Example: Diffusion Flux (Heat Flow)
                Superimpose the Total Heat
                \
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.4651510371048627`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"b962f39a-f4eb-4276-a8ae-\
8f1dbb42f543"],

Cell["\<\
It is possible to superimpose the total heat (related to the local \
temperature distribution) on the above animation.
The following animation is over a much longer time interval:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3b663c52-e0d3-4446-9ab8-7b8c5c4466a5"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"tempTotal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"t_", "/;", 
      RowBox[{"t", "<", ".2"}]}], "]"}], "=", "0"}], ";"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"tempTotal", "[", "t_", "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "10"], 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "10"], 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"uNew", "[", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], "]"}], 
      RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "x"}]}]}]}]}], ";"}]}], "InputOnly",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.39846290755*^9, 3.3984629077869997`*^9}, 
   3.398463029585*^9, {3.398463100415*^9, 3.398463120135*^9}},
